<blockquote class="uncited"><div>OK. Now it works. Simply switching off security settings have not been stored, but now there are active.<br>Now radio is recognized as "<strong class="text-strong">STM Device in DFU mode</strong>" and CPS is able to read and write data.<br>I wonder if I return security to recommended state and then to automatic driver installations it should still work.<br><br>Thank You so much.</div></blockquote><br>Update, I did not read the last update when I wrote this below . <br>But I still wonder what will happen in the long run as the support for the old DFU driver will be more and troublesome. <br><br>Did you install from the Windows 10 driver in <a href="https://www.opengd77.com/downloads/drivers/Dfuse_3.0.6_drivers.zip" class="postlink">downloads/drivers/Dfuse_3.0.6_drivers.zip</a>.<br>?<br><br>Is it 3.0.6 in properties on the driver? <br><br>Haven't seen such problem before but I guess we will get more and more problems with the DFU driver as STM doesn't maintain it anymore. <br><br>Seems that someone has to investigate how to use the revised STM driver in the CPS code or otherwise we are in trouble as Windows is "evolving"<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=2867">SA0BUX</a> — Fri Apr 25, 2025 3:00 pm</p><hr />
