<blockquote class="uncited"><div>Hello.<br>I have same / similar problem with newly purchased Baofeng DM1701.<br>Firmware version V002.006, CPS V01.05.<br>It came with programming cable.<br>CPS 1.05 doesn't see radio, radio is visible in Device Manager as Digital Radio in USB mode.<br>I tried to install usb driver dpinst_amd64.exe, but it didn't change anything.<br>I tried on two laptops. One with Win11 and second with Win10 - same behavior.<br><br>Is it common problem with DM1701 or just my radio is broken and I should return it and order another one from different shop?<br>I'd like to stay with factory firmware, but I need to enter my DMR ID number, which I could do only using CPS.<br>Radio is operational. I configured, using manu digital channel to work with my hotspot. I hear stations, but not able to transmit without DMR ID entered.<br><br>Pls help.</div></blockquote>Uninstall the "Digital Radio in USB mode" device  via the device manager, I suggest that you also tick the "Delete the driver software for this device".<br><br>Problem is that "Digital Radio in USB mode" driver match the same USB device id and outranks the older STM DFU driver.<br><br>On my Windows 11 laptop I have also disabled automatic driver update as Windows could reinstall the unwanted driver via Windows Update.<br><a href="https://pureinfotech.com/disable-automatic-driver-install-windows-11/" class="postlink">https://pureinfotech.com/disable-automa ... indows-11/</a><p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=2867">SA0BUX</a> — Fri Apr 25, 2025 8:06 am</p><hr />
]]></content>
